1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,337
Now watch a layout stop being a proposal and become a measurement.

2
00:00:04,287 --> 00:00:08,562
CoolSpend follows one rule: optimise, then validate.

3
00:00:08,562 --> 00:00:16,875
Let the fast, deterministic greedy engine choose the layout, then spend the expensive real simulations to find out what it actually does.

4
00:00:16,875 --> 00:00:18,512
Four steps.

5
00:00:18,512 --> 00:00:23,037
Build the demand field from a measured baseline UTCI field.

6
00:00:23,037 --> 00:00:26,800
Greedily place the trees where their shadows truly fall.

7
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:30,850
Run a live before-and-after simulation on the Infrared engine.

8
00:00:30,850 --> 00:00:34,725
Then report only the measured difference between the two grids.

9
00:00:34,725 --> 00:00:44,737
On this site, the greedy placed twenty trees: eight Tipuana tipu, five Styphnolobium japonicum, four Cercis siliquastrum, three Melia azedarach.

10
00:00:44,737 --> 00:00:46,812
Zero invasive.

11
00:00:46,812 --> 00:00:49,025
Zero London plane.

12
00:00:49,025 --> 00:00:56,412
Live calls are hard-capped at three per run, so one evaluation can never burn a runaway stack of paid simulations.

13
00:00:56,412 --> 00:00:58,750
And the result is the proof.

14
00:00:58,750 --> 00:01:04,225
Two thousand seven hundred and seventy-nine square metres cooled by at least half a degree.

15
00:01:04,225 --> 00:01:08,337
Two thousand two hundred and thirty-nine, by a full degree.

16
00:01:08,337 --> 00:01:11,300
Fourteen ninety-one, by two.

17
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:15,400
Mean felt-temperature drop, one point four eight degrees.

18
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:21,500
At the busiest sun-exposed cell, peak felt heat falls from thirty-one to thirty point six.

19
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:25,012
Seventy-two euros per square metre cooled.

20
00:01:25,012 --> 00:01:26,987
Not estimated.

21
00:01:26,987 --> 00:01:28,425
Measured.

